vironment Leadership and governance Strategic direction Vice-Chancellor University management Organisational structure Why Deakin Unbeatable employability History of excellence Top university rankings Education excellence Research excellence Indigenous education Values and culture Diversity, equity and inclusion Health and wellbeing Sustainability Modern slavery statement Careers at Deakin How to apply Why work at Deakin? News and media releases Study and career stories Learn more about Deakin Domestic or International Which best describes you? Domestic student You are an Australian domestic student if you are: an Australian citizen; an Australian permanent resident; an Australian permanent humanitarian visa holder; a New Zealand citizen. International student You are an international student if you are: a temporary resident (visa status) of Australia; a permanent resident (visa status) of New Zealand; a resident or citizen of any other country, intending to study on a\n            student visa. Reset Home Student life and services Support for high school students Career practitioners Support for high school students High school subject selection Year 12 to university Courses by ATAR Change of preference Parents and caregivers Career practitioners Deakin Accelerate Program Home Student life and services Support for high school students Career practitioners Career practitioners Help students make confident study decisions Support your students with trusted advice, practical resources and up-to-date information to help them explore study options and prepare for university. Support for high school students High school subject selection Year 12 to university Courses by ATAR Change of preference Parents and caregivers Career practitioners Deakin Accelerate Program Help your students achieve their career goals Choosing Deakin means choosing degrees that unlock real job outcomes. With work-integrated learning, industry connections and award-winning career services, we give your students the support they need to take the next step. Request to book a visit Submit a request for Deakin to visit your school, plan a student tour of our vibrant campuses or arrange an online presentation. Our Future Students team will review your submission and get in touch to explore available options. Request a school visit Download resources Find everything you need to help students choose a degree that leads to the kind of job they’ll love. Access the latest Careers Network News, undergraduate course guides and other Deakin publications. Browse resources Order a brochure or guide Use our publications order form to access the full range of brochures and guides that help students compare courses and explore career opportunities. Order a brochure Get the latest Deakin study and careers info Stay up to date with Careers Network News, annual mailouts and event invites – everything you need to help students create a clear plan for their future. Sign up Tools to support your students We’re here to help your students navigate Year 12, VTAC applications and the change of preference period with clarity and certainty. From exploring course options to managing deadlines, our expert guidance and practical tools help students make choices they feel good about. Explore courses by ATAR – Compare course options and discover where their ATAR could take them. ATAR Calculator – Estimate their ATAR and explore what it could mean for their study options. VCE Study Score Calculator – Predict raw and scaled study scores before results are released. Change of preference – Help students update their preferences with confidence and make informed course decisions. Access programs – Help more students get into university with Deakin's access and equity programs. Pathways finder – Discover flexible pathways into Deakin based on qualifications and study goals. Scholarships – Explore scholarships to help reduce the cost of university and reward achievement. Recommend Deakin Open Day to your students Deakin Open Day gives students the opportunity to explore our campuses, attend course presentations, chat with staff and students, and discover what university life is really like. It's a great way to help them make informed decisions about their future. Discover what's on Pathways and opportunities for your students Every student has a different journey to university. Whether they're high-achieving, eligible for adjusted entry or looking for an alternative pathway, Deakin offers programs that can help them reach their study goals. Join our Deakin Accelerate webinar Deakin Accelerate helps high-achieving Year 12 students get a head start on university. Register for our webinar on Wednesday 21 October to learn more about how the program can fast-track your students' path to university. Register now Deakin Guaranteed ATAR Do your students attend an under-represented school, live or study in a rural or regional area or come from an Indigenous background? Deakin offers lower guaranteed ATARs for eligible students, helping them feel more confident about securing a place in their desired course. Learn more about the Deakin Guaranteed ATAR Deakin Uni Ready If your students don't have an ATAR, Deakin Uni Ready could be the pathway for them. Free and online, it's a supported program that builds the academic skills and confidence they need to meet Deakin's entry requirements and step into a degree. Learn more about Deakin Uni Ready Meet our Future Students team Our Future Students team, based in Melbourne, Geelong and Warrnambool, is ready to support you with any questions or requests. Our Melbourne team Roula Karakostas Director, Future Students +61 3 9246 8067 Email Roula Luke Bryden Manager, Future Student Engagement +61 3 9244 5193 Email Luke Janine Kuster Manager, Future Student Pathways and Programs +61 3 9246 8035 Email Janine Luke Ridgwell Coordinator, Future Student Engagement +61 3 9246 8076 Email Luke Lauren Abel Coordinator, Future Student Engagement +61 3 9246 8359 Email Lauren Tara Dixon Coordinator, Pathways and Programs +61 3 9244 5903 Email Tara Pat Hearne Senior Officer, Future Student Engagement +61 3 9244 5071 Email Pat Sid Sharma Senior Officer, Future Student Engagement +61 3 9244 3077 Email Sid Belinda Wriedt Senior Officer, Future Student Engagement +61 3 9244 6006 Email Belinda Millie Sedlarevic Senior Officer, Future Student Engagement +61 3 9246 8118 Email Millie Nicollette Raftopoulos Senior Officer, Future Student Engagement +61 3 9246 8814 Email Nicollette Bec Lowery Senior Officer, Programs +61 4 3785 7328 Email Bec Our Geelong team Alex Campbell Coordinator, Future Student Engagement +61 3 5227 8996 Email Alex James Pountney Senior Officer, Future Student Engagement +61 3 9244 5949 Email James Natasha Fridey Senior Officer, Pathways and Programs +61 3 5227 2373 Email Natasha Our Warrnambool team Warrnambool (Please contact Future Students) Senior Officer, Future Student Engagement +61 3 9246 860 Email Future Students Tess McLeod Senior Officer, Future Student Engagement +61 3 5563 3130 Email Tess Rankings and footnotes Deakin references data from a range of government, higher education and reputable media sources. For more information, visit our University rankings page . Contact us Supporting your students starts with supporting you. Our expert advisers can help with course information, pathways, admissions and resources to make your career conversations easier. Contact us today. Email the Future Students Team Discover more Support for high school students Why Deakin Entry pathways Find a course by ATAR Was this page helpful? 1 - Lowest rating 2 - Low rating 3 - Neutral rating 4 - High rating 5 - Highest rating We use cookies to improve your experience. You consent to the use of our cookies if you proceed. Visit our Privacy policy for more information. OK Contact us Current students Future local students Future international students Research students Study at Deakin Find a course by ATAR Undergraduate courses Postgraduate courses Start an application Need help? Frequently asked questions Contact us Enquire online Student support services Research at Deakin Research degrees Find a research supervisor Research facilities Research news Top searches Scholarships Course guides How to apply Career stories Engagement at Deakin Partnership enquiry Event services Donate News and media Deakin University is known for strong outcomes in graduate\n            employment, course satisfaction, student support and quality\n            facilities. Explore our rankings . We acknowledge the Traditional Custodians of the unceded lands and\n            waterways on which Deakin University does business. We pay our deep\n            respect to the Ancestors and Elders of Wadawurrung Country, Eastern\n            Maar Country and Wurundjeri Country where our physical campuses are\n            located. We also acknowledge all First Nations Peoples that make\n            contributions to our learning communities. Find out how we support Indigenous inclusion at Deakin . Facebook Instagram LinkedIn TikTok YouTube WeChat - Deakin\n              University Sitemap Copyright Privacy Accessibility Disclaimer Safety and security © Copyright Deakin University 2026. Deakin University CRICOS Provider\n          Code: 00113B. TEQSA Provider ID PRV12124"
